        "content": "<p>I would like to create a PR for the following lemmas. </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">TFAE</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tfae_append_of_mem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">l₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ha</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l₁</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hb</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">TFAE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">l₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TFAE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TFAE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tfae_perm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">l₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l₁</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Perm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l₂</span><span class=\"o\">):</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">TFAE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TFAE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tfae_concat_of_mem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">TFAE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">concat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TFAE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Here are some questions.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Admittedly I don't know a lot about List, so I want to seek some advice on the best way to prove these lemmas. </li>\n<li>Suppose the approach above needs some lemmas about List (for example, right now I can't find a lemma saying that <code>(a :: l).Perm (l.concat a))</code>, but maybe it is just me not using searching tools correctly), and I want to add these lemmas. Which repository should I add these lemmas to? Mathlib or <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4\">https://github.com/leanprover/lean4</a>? I guess I can count myself as an experienced mathlib user but I have never made a PR to lean4, so any advice for making a succesful PR to lean4 is welcome!</li>\n</ol>",
